    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">The RTO registration certificate (RC) is a crucial document that needs to be provided. It is essential to make a photocopy of the RC and self-attest it as proof of ownership. Make sure the copy is clear and legible.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #10b98122; color: #10b981; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">02</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Current PUC:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Present a valid Pollution Under Control (PUC) certificate, which confirms that your vehicle meets the emission standards. This certificate is valid for a specific period, typically one month, and must be up-to-date.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Valid insurance certificate:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Provide a valid insurance certificate covering your car during the transport process. Make sure the insurance policy is up-to-date and covers the entire duration of the journey.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #a855f722; color: #a855f7; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">04</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">IBA-approved consignment bilty:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Obtain an Insurance Board of India (IBA) approved consignment bilty, which confirms the details of the transport such as the vehicle details, pick-up and drop locations, and contact information for both the sender and receiver.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<p>In addition to the aforementioned documents, please provide:</p>
	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Marine Transit Insurance:</strong> To ensure comprehensive protection for your vehicle during transportation, 100% declared-value marine transit insurance is highly recommended. This insurance policy covers your vehicle in case of any damages, theft, or accidents during transit.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Declaration Form:</strong> Fill out a declaration form, which clearly states the condition of your vehicle before and after the transportation process. This form helps establish the condition of your vehicle upon delivery and ensures fair compensation in case of any damages.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Vehicle Identity Card (VIC):</strong> If your car is more than 15 years old, you may need to provide a Vehicle Identity Card (VIC). The VIC serves as a proof of ownership and helps establish the vehicle's history.</span></li>
	</ul>

	<p>In addition to the above-mentioned paperwork, it is also important to:</p>
	<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 18px 0;">
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Clear All Dues:</strong> Ensure that you clear all outstanding dues and fees related to your vehicle before the transportation process.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Prepare Vehicle:</strong> Thoroughly check your vehicle for any damages or defects prior to transportation. It is advisable to clean the car to ensure a proper inspection.</span></li>
		<li style="margin-bottom: 10px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 5px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.95rem;"></i><span><strong>Signature of Receipt:</strong> Before the transportation process begins, make sure to sign the receipt provided by the car transport service provider, confirming that you have received your vehicle in good condition.</span></li>
	</ul></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



